  "progress_note": "R2/S1 remains accepted with clean focused and graphical evidence. R2/S2 graphical behavior is operator-confirmed. R2/S3 now also has real graphical evidence: the user supplied a first-person screenshot where individually articulated fingers are visibly rendered around the selected item, confirming that the Skeleton3D-driven procedural finger rig is active in the graphical lab. The separate S3 focused transcript was not pasted, so focused S3 is not retroactively invented; the S4 full runner revalidates all S2/S3 gates before the new S4 gates. S4 extends HeldItemGripProfileCatalog to schema v2 with a presentation-only two_hand contract: required, primary/secondary hand identity, secondary pose, secondary anchor transform and secondary hand transform, all metadata-overridable. The existing CH9.6 sandbox slot 2 item/mount-base is deliberately classified as the bounded two-hand graphical demonstration object while slot 1 beacon remains one-hand. TwoHandPosedFirstPersonEmbodiment temporarily reparents the left first-person hand under a secondary anchor attached to the current right-hand presentation proxy; the left hand is restored to its original viewmodel parent before the primary proxy is replaced or cleared, preventing hierarchy deletion and stale support poses. While secondary support is active, local Q-grab on the left hand fails closed with FPE_S4_SECONDARY_HAND_RESERVED. QuaterniusFirstPersonEmbodimentFix12 composes this behavior and exposes it in the debug HUD. Third-person still uses the accepted R2 right-hand world proxy; two-arm third-person IK is explicitly not claimed by S4. No accepted CH9.6 runtime file is modified.",
